commit bac11f8b5c7bc78e225423b0745a30584d9d38a7
Author: etonedemid <3damir0n3@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Jun 12 21:44:38 2026 -0300

    Enable SYSVIPC (ABI-safe) on ReSukiSU + SuSFS for Galaxy S25 (SM8750)
    
    - defconfig: CONFIG_SYSVIPC=y
    - sched.h: fold sysvsem/sysvshm into task_struct ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE slots
      (1 + 2 slots) instead of the mid-struct #ifdef block, so field offsets and
      genksyms CRCs stay byte-identical to stock GKI -> prebuilt vendor modules
      still load and the device boots (plain CONFIG_SYSVIPC=y bootloops).
    - Apply SuSFS overlay (susfs4ksu gki-android15-6.6) -> ReSukiSU inline hooks.
    - tools/lib/bpf: drop -Werror so resolve_btfids builds under newer clang.
    - Add build_sysvipc.sh + SYSVIPC_BUILD.md.
    
    Verified booting on Galaxy S25+ (pa2q) with working SysV IPC.

